# Testing

Every feature or bug fix ships with tests in the same change. Two test projects (xUnit v3):

| Project | Tools | Covers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `tests/Mostawsef.Api.IntegrationTests` | WebApplicationFactory + Testcontainers PostgreSQL (needs Docker) | Real HTTP endpoints, auth, validation, database, migrations |
| `tests/Mostawsef.Desktop.Tests` | Avalonia.Headless.XUnit (`[AvaloniaFact]`), `FakeApiHandler`, NSubstitute | View models, navigation/role guards, services, rendered views |

## Which test for which change

| Change | Required tests |
| --- | --- |
| New/changed API endpoint | Integration: success path, 400 (invalid input), 401 (no/invalid token), 403 (wrong role), 404/409 where relevant |
| Endpoint with a role policy | Integration: allowed role gets 2xx, every other role gets 403 |
| New entity / migration / constraint | Integration: data round-trips through the API; unique/required rules are enforced |
| Anything touching passwords, tokens, secrets | Integration: values are hashed/never returned (see `PasswordStorageTests`) |
| Business rule in Domain/Application | Integration through the endpoint that uses it (add a unit test only for complex pure logic) |
| New view model / command | Desktop: commands' CanExecute, success path, each `ApiError` shown to the user, loading state |
| New portal page or role | Desktop: allowed role can open it, other roles and signed-out users cannot (`NavigationGuardTests` pattern) |
| New view / layout change | Desktop: headless render test that the view appears with key texts; check Arabic (RTL) if layout-sensitive |
| New shared component with logic | Desktop: headless test of its behavior (properties -> visible state) |
| New user-visible string | Covered by the view model/view test asserting the English text; Arabic key must exist in `Strings.ar.resx` |
| Bug fix | A test that fails before the fix and passes after |

Skip tests only for pure styling/token changes and docs.

## Conventions
- Names describe behavior: `Wrong_password_returns_401`, `Admin_cannot_open_the_super_portal`.
- Folders mirror features: `Auth/`, later `Patients/`, `Appointments/`...
- API tests: `[Collection(ApiCollection.Name)]`, use `TestUsers` and `HttpClientExtensions` (`LoginAsAsync`, `WithBearer`).
  New seed data goes through `ApiFactory`; never depend on dev data.
- Desktop tests: `using var app = new TestServices();` (real DI, fake API, temp settings, English). Stub the server with
  `app.Api.RespondToLoginWith(...)`, `RespondWithStatus(...)`, `FailWithNetworkError()`; sign in with `app.SignInAs(role)`.
  Printouts never open a viewer in tests: `app.OpenedFiles` lists the PDFs the app asked to open.
- Time-dependent API behavior: swap the clock with `factory.WithWebHostBuilder(... ConfigureTestServices(s => s.AddSingleton<TimeProvider>(fixed)))`
  (see `ClockAndHealthTests`), never by sleeping.
- Never call the real API, real settings file or real database from desktop tests.
- Keep tests independent: no ordering, no shared mutable state between tests.

## Commands
Always use the script (it checks Docker and switches to Release when the app is running):
```powershell
./scripts/test.ps1 [all|api|desktop] [NameFilter] [-Watch] [-Coverage] [-Detailed]
./scripts/test.ps1 api Login
./scripts/test.ps1 desktop NavigationGuard -Watch
```

CI (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`) runs `./scripts/test.ps1 api` on Ubuntu and `./scripts/test.ps1 desktop` on Windows
on every push. API tests must stay OS-neutral (no Windows-only paths or APIs); a red CI run blocks "done".
